From: OpenWrt community <openwrt-devel@lists.openwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: ignore association regulatory hints

Ignore country information elements and disconnect regulatory hints so
association changes do not replace the system regulatory configuration.

Original author was not recorded in the imported patch.
[viking.yfy@qq.com: complete imported patch metadata]
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/net/wireless/reg.c
+++ b/net/wireless/reg.c
@@ -3352,6 +3352,8 @@ void regulatory_hint_country_ie(struct w
 	enum environment_cap env = ENVIRON_ANY;
 	struct regulatory_request *request = NULL, *lr;
 
+	return;
+
 	/* IE len must be evenly divisible by 2 */
 	if (country_ie_len & 0x01)
 		return;
@@ -3601,6 +3603,7 @@ static bool is_wiphy_all_set_reg_flag(en
 
 void regulatory_hint_disconnect(void)
 {
+	return;
 	/* Restore of regulatory settings is not required when wiphy(s)
 	 * ignore IE from connected access point but clearance of beacon hints
 	 * is required when wiphy(s) supports beacon hints.
